{"id":"ni43101:26e35c43a32381d1","archive_url":"https://github.com/jaydeepdive/minemodelingpro/releases/download/report-archive/ni43101_26e35c43a32381d1.pdf","report_url":"https://minedocs.com/22/Asanko-TR-02282022.pdf","company":"Asanko","project":"Asanko","commodity":"Au","jurisdiction":"Ghana","date":"2026-10-27","title_project":"Asanko","cover_company":"Galiano Gold Inc","extractor":"dt21","extracted":"2026-10-27T12:03:33Z","pages":431,"crs":{"zone":30,"hemi":"N","datum":"WGS84","zone_votes":{"30":1},"kind":"local"},"center":[6.3278,-2.0153],"text_center":[6.3278,-2.0153],"block_size":[5.0,5.0,3.0],"density":2.68,"sensitivity":null,"extent":{"strike":{"n":5,"min":250.0,"max":1000.0,"median":600.0,"page":105,"text":"part of the vein system is 15 m to 20 m wide, but it tapers to about 10 m at both ends; the vein system has a strike length of about 700 m although the main area of economic significance is the cent"},"depth":{"n":3,"min":50.0,"max":250.0,"median":150.0,"page":68,"text":"tely reviewed and expanded project scope. Further RC and DDH drilling conducted to increase Mineral Resources to a depth of 150 m at Nkran and to further assess the known mineralization at"}},"attitude":{"dip":{"n":2,"median":80.0,"min":75.0,"max":80.0,"page":97,"text":"A granite intrusion surrounds a 080\u00b0 dipping cross structure and mineralization hosted in bounding"},"dip_direction":{"n":6,"median":315.0,"min":90.0,"max":315.0,"page":78,"text":"olded and sheared, and generally dip steeply to the north-west at between 70\u00ba to 80\u00ba, with a steep"}},"geophysics":{"surveys":[{"method":"magnetics","page":39,"text":"2022 Page 6 Geophysical surveys over the property have included regional aeromagnetic imaging of the Ashanti Belt and adjacent Kumasi Basin by the Ghana Geological Survey, as well as induced potential (IP) ground geophysical su","platform":"airborne","year":2022},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":39,"text":"well as induced potential (IP) ground geophysical surveying and airborne VTEM and magnetic survey centred over specific targets.","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"magnetics","page":54,"text":"States Dollars VRA Volta River Authority VTEM Versatile Time-Domain Electromagnetic Surveying WBSZ Western Bounding Shear Zone WNW West-North-West WOX Weakly-Oxidized WRD Waste Rock Dump WRDF Waste Rock Dump Facility XRD X-Ray Di","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"magnetics","page":69,"text":"PMI also completed a VTEM electromagnetic (EM) and magnetic survey centred over the Nkran pit. Previous Owner 2015-2016 Nkran Mine dewatered and re-opened by Asanko Gold as a deeper opencast operation.","platform":"airborne","year":2011},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":69,"text":"PMI also completed a VTEM electromagnetic (EM) and magnetic survey centred over the Nkran pit.","platform":"airborne","year":2011,"line_km":2266.0},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":111,"text":"areas of exposure \u2022 3,000-line kilometre heli-borne versatile time-domain electromagnetic surveying (VTEM) survey infilling previous gaps in coverage \u2022 Updated regional geological interpretation based on the interpretation of th","platform":"airborne","line_km":3000.0},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":112,"text":"28, 2022 Page 79 Figure 9-1 Regional Geological Interpretation from VTEM Survey Source: Asanko Gold Mine, 2021","platform":"airborne","year":2022},{"method":"magnetics","page":117,"text":"Surveys Geophysical surveys over the property have included regional aeromagnetic imaging of the Ashanti Belt and adjacent Kumasi Basin by the Ghana Geological Survey, as well as IP ground geophysical surveying and airborne","platform":"airborne","year":2015},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":117,"text":"Geological Survey, as well as IP ground geophysical surveying and airborne VTEM and magnetic survey centred over specific targets.","platform":"airborne","year":2015},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":119,"text":"over the Esaase deposit are as follows: \u2022 Gradient array IP \u2022 Pole-dipole resistivity \u2022 HaiTEM MLEM (electromagnetic) \u2022 Gravity."},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":119,"text":"Eleven Gradient Array blocks and six 2D Pole-dipole lines were read over the Esaase project for a total of 6,700-line metres."},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":120,"text":"However, the global pandemic in 2020-2021 delayed commencement of this activity.","year":2020},{"method":"magnetics","page":123,"text":"Romex also completed geochemical surveys including stream sediment sampling, rock chip sampling, and soil"},{"method":"radiometrics","page":123,"text":"exploration including a VTEM survey which included acquisition of a DTM, radiometrics, aeromagnetics and electromagnetic (resistivity).","platform":"airborne","year":2022}],"targets":[{"page":38,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"Quartz veins and disseminated sulphides are hosted in rocks ranging from granite and tonalite to sandstone, siltstone, and shale."},{"page":422,"explained":false,"untested":true,"text":"In addition, deep IP should be considered at deposits such as Abore to explore for chargeability features that may indicate extensions to mineralization at depth and assist in more efficient drill targeting."}]},"rock":{"weathering_m":{"n":1,"min":40.0,"max":40.0,"median":40.0,"page":68,"text":"The broad, low-lying Nkran had relief of only about 40 m with oxidation extending to depths of 40 m. Previous Owner 1995 Additional DDH, RC, RC and RCD drilling was completed."},"density_samples":{"n":3,"min":1.0,"max":16687.0,"median":53.0,"page":143,"text":"Mine, Ashanti Region, Ghana Effective Date: February 28, 2022 Page 110 11.2.1.1 Bulk Density Measurements Esaase bulk density measurements were collected over a range of lithological and weathered profiles."},"rqd":{"n":1,"min":0.0,"max":0.0,"median":0.0,"page":183,"text":"are not merged until corrected \u2022 Geotechnical tables: Core recoveries and rock quality designations (RQDs) less than 0%, or greater